A fiber that runs a function which forks one in which a writer runs and then one that masks (also through a lambda over a helper's own function parameter), a helper that leaves a writer and a reader running and a mask after it, a scope closed with a masked finaliser after its function forked such a fiber, and a scope that runs such a function within; each update writes a copy of the contents, accepted (ownership-v3-kernel.md §13 item 12, *A defect*, (d), *After such a call*, *Descendants of a masked fiber*, `Contract.runs_on`, #2653). Its live twin is CellScopeCloseLive.
